<title>COLOMBIA: Colombian peso edges back against dollar.</title>
<headline>Colombian peso edges back against dollar.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's peso won back 10 centavos to close  at 1,112.90, interbank dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said banks shortening dollar positions buoyed the peso, which  they forecast would continue to rise through next week.</p>
<p>Dealers reported 265 trades worth $147 million, slightly below the  daily average. The peso opened at 1,113.20 and traded between an intraday  high of 1,112.15 and a low of 1,114.90.</p>
<p>((-- Nelson Bocanegra, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
